.TH VEIL 1 "September 2026" "veil @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
veil \- general purpose steganography toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B veil
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.I subcommand
.RI [ arguments ]
.PP
.B veil encode
.I target
.I data
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.RB [ \-verify ]
.PP
.B veil decode
.I target
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.PP
.B veil help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B veil
hides arbitrary data inside a carrier file and recovers it again.
PNG carriers store the data in the least significant bits of the pixels,
JPEG carriers store it in the DCT coefficients.
.PP
Both
.B encode
and
.B decode
prompt for a passphrase.
When one is given the payload is encrypted before it is embedded, and the
passphrase also seeds where in the carrier the payload is placed.
Leave the prompt empty to store the data unencrypted.
The same passphrase must be given to decode it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print debug output.
Must come before the subcommand.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "encode " "target data"
Hide the contents of
.I data
inside the PNG or JPEG image
.I target
and write the result to a new file.
The target itself is left untouched.
If
.I data
is
.BR \- ,
the data is read from standard input and the passphrase is read from
.IR /dev/tty .
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Where to write the carrier holding the data.
Defaults to
.IR output.bin .
.TP
.B \-verify
Decode the written file again and check it holds the same data.
.RE
.TP
.BI "decode " target
Recover the data hidden inside
.I target
and write it to a file.
The passphrase is read from standard input.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Where to write the recovered data, or
.B \-
for standard output.
Defaults to
.IR output.bin .
Decoding a file into itself is refused.
.RE
.TP
.B help
List the available subcommands.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Bad usage, an unknown subcommand, or a failed encode or decode.
.SH EXAMPLES
Hide a file in an image:
.PP
.RS
.EX
veil encode photo.png secret.txt \-o photo\-out.png \-verify
.EE
.RE
.PP
Get it back:
.PP
.RS
.EX
veil decode photo\-out.png \-o secret.txt
.EE
.RE
.PP
Pipe data in and out:
.PP
.RS
.EX
tar c notes/ | veil encode photo.jpg \- \-o photo\-out.jpg
veil decode photo\-out.jpg \-o \- | tar x
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/IdanKoblik/veil
.UE
